Dear API User,

As part of our API Security Enhancement Program, your API keys will be
rotated in 72 hours. This is a mandatory security measure.

Affected API Keys:
  AbC3xY...9fK2  (HMAC-SHA256, created 2024-11-08)  - Expiring
  XyZ7pQ...3mN8  (Ed25519, created 2025-03-22)       - Expiring

How to rotate your API keys:

  1. Open your browser and navigate to binance.com manually
  2. Log in with your email and 2FA
  3. Go to Account → API Management → Create New API Key
  4. Replace the old keys in your trading system with the new ones
  5. Delete the old keys

  API endpoint remains: https://api.binance.com
  (No endpoint change is needed. If an email tells you to use a new
  API endpoint, it is a phishing attempt.)

Impact on automated trading:
  Trading bots: Must update keys before expiry. Open positions preserved.
  WebSocket streams: Active connections terminated. Reconnect with new keys.
  Withdrawal whitelist: IP entries preserved but must be re-verified.
  Sub-accounts: Must be rotated individually by master account.

Security note:
Binance will NEVER:
  - Send you a direct link to rotate API keys
  - Ask you to use a new API endpoint from an email
  - Ask for your API secret key via email
  - Use a non-binance.com domain for API operations

If you receive an email directing you to a "rotation portal" or a "new
API endpoint," it is a phishing attempt. Always access API management
by navigating to binance.com manually in your browser.

If your trading system uses a non-UTF-8 character encoding (e.g., GB2312),
please ensure it is updated to UTF-8 to avoid rendering issues with API
responses.

